# Office UI events (mandatory when `.aisdlc/` exists)

If the workspace has `.aisdlc/` (created by `ai-sdlc --init`), **every agent turn that starts or finishes real work MUST emit an event** so the office board stays live.

## Command (prefer portable script — no pip required)

```bash
python3 .cursor/scripts/office-event.py --agent <agent-id> --status <status> --task "<short task>" --phase <phase>
```

Fallback if `ai-sdlc` is on PATH:

```bash
ai-sdlc event --agent <agent-id> --status <status> --task "<short task>" --phase <phase>
```

## Status values

| Status | When |
|--------|------|
| `working` | Agent begins the task |
| `waiting` | Blocked on human/judge/upstream |
| `done` | Task finished successfully |
| `error` | Task failed |
| `idle` | Clear desk after handoff (empty `--task`) |

## Who emits

| Actor | `--agent` value |
|-------|------------------|
| Orchestrator / planner | `architect-planner` |
| Scaffold | `scaffold-agent` |
| Design | `designer-worker` |
| Backend | `backend-worker` |
| Frontend | `frontend-worker` |
| Database | `database-worker` |
| QA | `qa-worker` |
| Security | `security-worker` |
| DevOps | `devops-worker` |
| Judge | `judge-agent` |
| Learning | `learning-agent` |
| Spike / contract | `spike-agent` / `contract-agent` |

## Minimum cadence

1. **Start of turn** → `working` + task one-liner + phase  
2. **End of turn** → `done` or `error`  
3. **Handoff / idle** → `idle` with empty task  

Orchestrator running `/dev-module` emits on **every phase transition** (see command file). Workers emit even if orchestrator already emitted for the phase.

## Do not

- Skip emits because the UI is not open (still write the log)
- Invent agent ids not in `.cursor/agents/`
- Print secrets/PII in `--task` / `--detail`
